\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{6}{Three-layer architecture of \psychbench {}. Benchmarks define experimental paradigms with HDC-encoded stimuli. The harness provides psychometric infrastructure (reliability, SAT curves, normative comparison, neuromodulator profiles). The reporting layer generates self-contained analysis outputs. Arrows indicate data flow from the agent under test upward through encoding, evaluation, and reporting}{figure.caption.11}{}}
